{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1551402-turning-someone-into-quintessence","id":1551402,"title":"Turning someone into Quintessence","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-06-01T20:16:10-07:00","id":1551402,"title":"Turning someone into Quintessence","content":"So, that's the question, have you ever wondered about an effect like turning someone into Quintessence and absorbing him/her?<br /> Would only Prime be enough or Life (and Matter or Spirits, for vampires and werewolves, etc) also?<br /> <br /> I was wondering about it myself. Any contribution is welcomed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-01T21:05:24-07:00","id":1551406,"title":"","content":"I believe direct conversion of living beings into Quintessence requires only Prime 5. I think undead would count as such rather than as inanimate objects since they're sentient and have some sort of animating spiritual energy (though not necessarily life force in the case of zombies and Risen).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-01T21:15:19-07:00","id":1551407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1551402-turning-someone-into-quintessence?p=1551406#post1551406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe direct conversion of living beings into Quintessence requires only Prime 5. I think undead would count as such rather than as inanimate objects since they're sentient and have some sort of animating spiritual energy (though not necessarily life force in the case of zombies and Risen).</div> </div> </div> </div>I see, I say that because in late Mage suplements it was made much harder to affect Vampire patterns. Someone asked me how would one turn another creature into Quintessence and absorb it into himself, so I started thinking about it, I don't know if I should count the Cainite's blood or the Werewolf Gnosis as &quot;extra&quot; Quintessence in this &quot;absurdly powerful spell&quot;, as the idea is not only to desintegrate another creature but ALSO turn it into Quintessence AND absorb it into himself. So, one could say a normal human would be worth 7 Quintessence for a Mage, but what about a powerful vampire. What about the damage, would we follow the normal damage chart (i.e. 1 sucess = 1, 2 = 2, 3 = 6, 3 = 8, 5 =10, 6 =18, etc). There are so many questions...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-02T06:41:40-07:00","id":1551414,"title":"","content":"In M20, it takes extra spheres to affect other supernaturals. It really only covers direct damage, but Vampires are Life 3/Matter 2, Werecreatures are Life 3/Spirit 2, and Fae are Life 3/Mind 3(2?). Now it is unclear if that is supposed to scale or not. That is, it is unclear if a Life 5 spell on a vampire would need Matter 2 or Matter 4. Unfortunately the one example we have of a high level Life spell on a vampire is so maliciously written it isn't helpful (the Vampire Lawn Chair).<br /> <br /> That doesn't matter too much for Vampires in this case as pulling the quintessence from a matter pattern is Prime 4, so a Master of Prime can cover both the living and unliving sides of draining a Vampire. For the others, it is an ST call.<br /> <br /> You are on the right track with treating this as a damage spell where the damage done is also the quintessence gathered. Whether it follows the normal spell damage progression or only does 1 damage per success is an ST call.<br /> <br /> I would say that converting the target's power supply is a different (though possibly related) effect to dissolving and consuming their pattern. The form this takes is going to depend on the power source. Vitae has an actual physical presence and can stick around so a mage can probably treat it like a complicated form of Tass. Gnosis would need to be drained and converted directly, I think.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-06T01:37:15-07:00","id":1551497,"title":"","content":"I think a living human is worth 10 Quint, just as they're worth 10 Vitae despite death coming before all of it is drained. You can assume that the last 3 points are from the corpse itself. Turning a victim that has previously been drained by a Vampire would deduce the Vitae taken from the Quint they're worth, even to the point that a completely drained body can't really be absorbed as Quint at all.<br /> <br /> But while there's nothing stopping such an effect, what may be a concern is its effect on the Mage's Resonance. This is a very direct form of cannibalism, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-06T15:31:52-07:00","id":1551505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1551402-turning-someone-into-quintessence?p=1551414#post1551414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I<br /> <br /> That doesn't matter too much for Vampires in this case as pulling the quintessence from a matter pattern is Prime 4, so a Master of Prime can cover both the living and unliving sides of draining a Vampire. For the others, it is an ST call.<br /> <br /> You are on the right track with treating this as a damage spell where the damage done is also the quintessence gathered. Whether it follows the normal spell damage progression or only does 1 damage per success is an ST call.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Isnt transforming things into quintessence Prime 2? You just cant absorb it at this level. 4 allows to burn quintessence inside a living being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-06T17:13:18-07:00","id":1551507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1551402-turning-someone-into-quintessence?p=1551406#post1551406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe direct conversion of living beings into Quintessence requires only Prime 5. I think undead would count as such rather than as inanimate objects since they're sentient and have some sort of animating spiritual energy (though not necessarily life force in the case of zombies and Risen).</div> </div> </div> </div>Prime 5 doesn't turn anyone into quintessence, what it does is release the quintessence from their pattern, which as a result, gives them a sudden existence failure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-07T10:46:38-07:00","id":1551515,"title":"","content":"To-may-to, to-mah-to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-15T15:26:35-07:00","id":1551695,"title":"","content":"Vampires are easy; Blood = Quintessence; take their blood/quintessence away, they no longer function.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}